hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1643","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn ‘Abdah and also narrated to us Ziyad ibn Ayyub, both said: Narrated to us Isma‘il, they both said: Narrated to us ‘Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, who said:\nA young man stood up before ‘Imran ibn Husayn and took hold of the reins of his riding animal, then asked him about the prayer during travel. So ‘Imran turned to us and said:\n“This young man is asking me about a matter, and I would love to relate it to all of you.\nI went out on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he never prayed anything but two rak‘ahs at a time until he returned to Madinah.”\nZiyad ibn Ayyub added:\n“I also performed Hajj with him, and he did not pray anything but two rak‘ahs until he returned to Madinah.”\nBoth of them said:\n“He stayed in Makkah for eighteen nights during the Conquest and prayed two rak‘ahs at a time, then he said to the people of Makkah:\n‘Pray four rak‘ahs, for we are a people on a journey.’\nI also went out on military expeditions with Abu Bakr and performed Hajj with him, and he never prayed anything but two rak‘ahs until he returned.\nI performed Hajj with ‘Umar several times, and he never prayed anything but two rak‘ahs until he returned.\n‘Uthman also prayed two rak‘ahs during Hajj for seven years of his caliphate until he returned to Madinah, then after that he prayed four rak‘ahs.”\nAhmad’s version adds:\n“Then he said: ‘Have I made it clear to you?’\nWe said: ‘Yes.’”\nThe wording of the hadith is that of Ahmad ibn ‘Abdah.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
